  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/validate.cc",
    "description": "In ValidateArrayDataVisitor::Visit(const UnionArray&), union type codes are validated with `if (code < 0 || child_ids[code] == kInvalidChildId)`, but there is no upper-bound check that `code < child_ids.size()` (or <=255). A malformed IPC stream can produce an out-of-range positive type code, causing `child_ids[code]` to read past bounds (ASan reports global-buffer-overflow). Crash is observed at validate.cc:356 during full record batch validation.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer input is parsed by ipc::internal::FuzzIpcStream into a RecordBatch, then RecordBatch::ValidateFull() calls internal::ValidateArrayData recursively. The PoV must construct a UnionArray (here reachable through nested list validation) with non-null entries and a raw type_codes buffer containing a positive code not present in the union type\u2019s child_ids mapping. During Visit(UnionArray), dereferencing child_ids[code] without bounds checking triggers OOB read."
  },
